{"name":"El Dorado","hex":"#a97f3c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"El Dorado","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A Muisca tribal chief who covered himself in gold dust.","A legendary lost city of gold."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/El_Dorado"}],"entries":[{"title":"El Dorado","blocks":[{"text":"El Dorado is a mythical city of gold supposedly located somewhere in South America. The legend originated in 16th-century Spanish accounts of a ruler known as El Dorado, or the Golden One, who was said to cover himself in gold dust before washing it off in a sacred lake. Over time, the name came to refer not only to the ruler, but also to a lost city or kingdom of immense wealth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Laguna_de_Guatavita_centro_de_la_leyenda_del_Dorado.jpg/330px-Laguna_de_Guatavita_centro_de_la_leyenda_del_Dorado.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Dorado"},{"title":"El Dorado (Shakira album)","blocks":[{"text":"El Dorado is the eleventh studio album by Colombian singer-songwriter Shakira, released on 26 May 2017, by Sony Music Latin. The album is mainly sung in Spanish, with three songs in English. After her self-titled tenth studio album (2014), Shakira had her second child, suffered from writer's block and was uncertain about the future of her career. However, her collaboration on \"La Bicicleta\" with Carlos Vives, encouraged Shakira to continue to work on music."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a7/Shakira_El_Dorado_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Dorado_(Shakira_album)"},{"title":"Dorado","blocks":[{"text":"Dorado is a constellation in the Southern Sky. It was named in the late 16th century and is now one of the 88 modern constellations. Its name refers to the mahi-mahi, which is known as dorado (\"golden\") in Spanish, although it has also been depicted as a swordfish. Dorado contains most of the Large Magellanic Cloud, the remainder being in the constellation Mensa. The South Ecliptic pole also lies within this constellation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Dorado_IAU.svg/330px-Dorado_IAU.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dorado"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Don_Gonzalo_Jim%C3%A9nez_de_Quesada.JPG/500px-Don_Gonzalo_Jim%C3%A9nez_de_Quesada.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Don_Gonzalo_Jim%C3%A9nez_de_Quesada.JPG/500px-Don_Gonzalo_Jim%C3%A9nez_de_Quesada.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gonzalo Jiménez de Quesada","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADon_Gonzalo_Jim%C3%A9nez_de_Quesada.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Muisca_tunjo_-_MET_-_Art._DT6752.jpg/500px-Muisca_tunjo_-_MET_-_Art._DT6752.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Muisca_tunjo_-_MET_-_Art._DT6752.jpg/1280px-Muisca_tunjo_-_MET_-_Art._DT6752.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Muisca_tunjo_-_MET_-_Art._DT6752.jpg/500px-Muisca_tunjo_-_MET_-_Art._DT6752.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Muisca tunjo","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMuisca_tunjo_-_MET_-_Art._DT6752.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Gold_Museum%2C_Bogota_%2836145671394%29.jpg/500px-Gold_Museum%2C_Bogota_%2836145671394%29.jpg?utm_source=e